  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/c51e6206f77b63181f6c9f67b116ba5c0024886c061e8c15fe10edab87c87e03.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ at the point $x=3$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(3)\u2248$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)\u2248\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=3.$ Applying the above formula with $x=3$ and $h=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(3) & \u2248\\frac{f(3+2)-f(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(5)-f(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-5}{2} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
